@@ -15,3 +15,20 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in, sign-up and account settings support passkeys (WebAuthn) via [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/):
+
+- **Sign up** (`/signup`): passkey-first account creation, with a password fallback. Password sign-ups are offered a passkey right after registering.
+- **Sign in** (`/signin`): passkey autofill on the username field (conditional mediation), a "Sign in with a passkey" button, and an automatic passkey upgrade (conditional create) after a password sign-in.
+- **Account settings** (`/account`): list, add, rename and remove passkeys. Adding or removing a passkey requires a recent sign-in (5 minutes); otherwise the user confirms with a passkey or password first. The WebAuthn Signal API keeps password managers in sync.
+
+Passwords are still verified by the external auth service. The Astro server proxies those requests (`/api/auth/login`, `/api/auth/register`) so it can set a session. Passkey credentials are stored in a JSON file. Configuration:
+
+| Env var | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `AUTH_DATA_DIR` | `./.data` | Where the account/passkey store is written |
+| `PASSKEY_RP_ID` | request hostname | WebAuthn Relying Party ID |
+| `PASSKEY_ORIGINS` | request origin | Comma-separated list of allowed origins |
+| `AUTH_API_BASE` | Cloud Functions URL | External password auth service |
